The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
info = platform_get_drvdata(dev);
if (!info)
```
Reason:
The function `platform_get_drvdata(dev)` is expected to return a valid pointer to the device data associated with the platform device. If it returns `NULL`, the subsequent code does not handle this case properly, leading to the function exiting without an error code, which can result in undefined behavior or incorrect handling in the calling code.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!info) {
    err = -EINVAL;
    goto out;
}
```
Reason:
This code checks if `info` is `NULL` and assigns an error code `-EINVAL` to `err` if it is. This ensures that the function properly indicates an error condition when there is no valid device data, allowing the calling code to handle the error appropriately.

